    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="0705" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12963.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-22T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please call upon Carranza personally if possible, otherwise on Foreign Office,
                    and urge the avoidance of anything which could be construed as a lack of
                    courtesy to the diplomatic representatives. It is very important that whatever
                    he finds it necessary to do should be done with due regard to diplomatic usage
                    and respect to the diplomatic character of foreign representatives. Airy other
                    course of action might involve him in serious foreign complications.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
